# FullVue marketing copy

Read **fullvue-io-marketing-agent.md** for the full brief. This repo is the fullvue.io **marketing site**; ERP paths in that doc refer to the product codebase.

## Hard rules

- **Assets** replaces legacy **Equipment** and **IT Database (ITDB)** — one module, slug `assets`. Do not list Equipment/ITDB as separate product modules on this site.
- Match **module names** to the catalog titles: Accounting, AI, Assets, Attendance, Core, Counter, Email, Human Resources, Production Meetings, Invoicing, Planner, Products, Purchasing, Rentals, Field, Sales, SDS, SMS, Customer Support, Tether, To-Dos.
- **Outcome-first** copy for owners/GMs; no unsupported superlatives or invented integrations.
- **Accounting** is an in-app GL. **QuickBooks Online** is a separate one-way push of invoices, credit memos, bills, and payments—not two-way sync, not a QBO replacement.
- **AI** is a deployment module (`ai`) marketed at `/modules/ai`. The assistant name **Ask FullVue** is fine in body copy. Do not claim write mode. Metered AI credits—not a priced checkbox on `/pricing`. `/ai` redirects to `/modules/ai`.
- Primary CTA is **Start free trial** → `/trial` (auto-provisioning). Use `/contact` for questions—not as the default conversion CTA.
- **SMS** is a distinct deployment module (`sms`). List it on the hub and `/modules/sms`. Do not invent a calculator price; use “Talk to us” until a posted rate exists.
- Industry pages may mention equipment in plain English; product/module lists must use **Assets**.

## Site gaps to watch

Accounting, AI, Email, SMS, Counter, Assets, Rentals, Tether, Planner, Attendance — flag if missing from `/modules` or pricing.
